Here's a solution for your problem using TypedArray and bitwise operations:

```javascript
function packEntities(entities) {
  const buffer = new Uint16Array(Math.ceil(entities.length / 2));

  let offset = 0;
  for (let i = 0; i < entities.length; i++) {
    const entity = entities[i];
    const id = entity.id & 0xF; // masking to get 4 bits
    const size = (entity.size & 0x7) << 3; // shifting and masking to get 3 bits

    buffer[offset] |= (id << 12) | (size << 8); // packing id and size into one 16-bit value
    offset++;

    if (offset === buffer.length) break; // if we've reached the end of the buffer, break the loop
  }

  return buffer.buffer;
}

function unpackEntities(buffer, length) {
  const entities = [];
  const view = new DataView(buffer);

  for (let i = 0; i < length; i += 2) {
    const entity = { id: 0, size: 0 };

    entity.id = view.getUint16(i, true) >> 12; // shifting to get id
    entity.size = (view.getUint16(i, true) >> 8) & 0x7; // masking to get size

    entities.push(entity);
  }

  return entities;
}
```

In the `packEntities` function, we create a Uint16Array buffer and pack multiple entities into it. We use bitwise operations to pack the id and size into a single 16-bit value.

In the `unpackEntities` function, we create a DataView from the provided ArrayBuffer and unpack the entities from it. We use bitwise operations to extract the id and size from the packed 16-bit values.

